==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{term|dies|diēs|day|lang=la}} and {{term|Mercurii|lang=la}}, genitive of {{term|Mercurius||Mercury|lang=la}}.
Latin calque of Koine Greek ἡμέρα Ἕρμου ''heméra Hérmou''. The association of the seven week days with the seven classical planets is first attested in the ''Anthologiarum'' by [[:w:Vettius Valens|Vettius Valens]], ca. AD 170 and was known to Cassius Dio by the early 3rd century.

